{"book":26,"chapter":26,"context":{"chapter":26,"title":"Tyre, a Rock for Nets","summary":"Because Tyre cheered Jerusalem's fall as a business opportunity, God says many nations will come against it like waves, beginning with Nebuchadnezzar, until it is a bare rock where fishermen dry their nets.","background":"Tyre was a wealthy Phoenician trading city, partly built on an island just off the coast. According to the historian Josephus, Nebuchadnezzar besieged it for thirteen years but did not destroy the island city, something Ezekiel himself acknowledges later (29:17-20). In 332 BC Alexander the Great built a causeway to the island and sacked it.","customs":[{"term":"Spreading of nets","verses":"26:5","note":"Fishermen laid nets out on flat rocks to dry and mend them. A proud city reduced to a drying rack is a picture of complete ruin."}],"watchFor":["Tyre's motive: 'Aha... I shall be replenished' (v. 2).","The shift from 'he' (Nebuchadnezzar, vv. 7–11) to 'they' (v. 12).","The coastal princes' lament (vv. 16–18)."],"connections":["Isaiah 23:1-18","Amos 1:9-10","Joel 3:4-8","Ezekiel 29:17-20"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["בְּעַשְׁתֵּי","be'ashtei-","H6249","HR/Acbsa","in one [plus]"],["עֶשְׂרֵה","'esreh","H6240","HAcbsa","ten"],["שָׁנָה","shanah","H8141","HNcfsa","year"],["בְּאֶחָד","be'echad","H259","HR/Acfsa","on [day] one"],["לַחֹדֶשׁ","lachodesh","H2320","HRd/Ncmsa","of the month"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["דְבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] word of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֵלַי","'elai","H413","HR/Sp1bs","to me"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]],"x":[[26020001,26020001,3]],"xn":1},"2":{"w":[["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","O son of"],["אָדָם","'adam","H120","HNcmsa","humankind"],["יַעַן","ya'an","H3282","HC","because"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher-","H834","HTr","that"],["אָמְרָה","'amerah","H559","HVqp3fs","it said"],["צֹּר","tzor","H6865","HNpl","Tyre"],[